  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Let $P={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},\u2026,{x}_{m}}$ be a partition of the interval $[4,11].$ If $\u0394{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}\u0394{x}_{i}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Note that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}\u0394{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[4,11],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}\u0394{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+\u22ef+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+\u22ef+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =11-4 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
